### [MODIFY] [socket_events.js](file:///c:/github/textline/static/js/socket_events.js)

**What changes**: Add Monitor state persistence to `sessionStorage` whenever key events fire.

1. Define `MONITOR_STATE_KEY = 'textline_monitor_state_v1'`.
2. After `status_update` handler updates DOM (or would update DOM if elements existed), **also** save the critical state to `sessionStorage`:
   - `status` (processing/success/error/idle)
   - `answer` (the full answer text)
   - `message` (status message)
   - `timestamp`
   - `metadata` (full provenance object)
   - `pipeline_id`
   - `activeRouteStr` (the computed route string)
3. After `image_preview` handler, save `imageUrl` to the same state object.
4. After `pipeline_log` handler, append the log entry data to a `pipelineLogs` array in the state (capped at 200 entries).
5. Use a helper `saveMonitorState(updates)` that merges updates into the existing state and writes once.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This runs on ALL pages (socket_events.js loads via base.html). Even when on `/health`, if a `status_update` arrives, it persists the Monitor state to `sessionStorage`. This is the key mechanism that handles "navigation during processing".

