### [NEW] [monitor_restore.js](file:///c:/github/textline/static/js/monitor_restore.js)

**What it does**: Restores Monitor DOM state from `sessionStorage` when `/monitor` loads.

1. Reads `textline_monitor_state_v1` from `sessionStorage`.
2. If valid state exists with `status === 'success'`:
   - Sets `#preview-image.src` and shows the image / hides placeholder.
   - Sets `#answer-text.textContent` and shows it / hides placeholder.
   - Shows `#copy-btn`.
   - Restores provenance panel fields (`#prov-provider-model`, `#prov-key-id`, `#prov-fallback`, etc.).
   - Shows `#provenance-container`.
   - Restores `#active-route-display` text and color.
   - Restores `#status-badge` to "SUCCESS".
   - Restores `#status-provenance-tag`.
3. If state has `status === 'processing'`:
   - Shows processing indicators.
   - The live Socket.IO connection will deliver fresh events that update normally.
4. If state has `status === 'error'`:
   - Restores error message and badge.
5. Restores pipeline log entries from `pipelineLogs` array into `#pipeline-log-console`.
6. Restores `#pipeline-id-badge` text.
7. Restores `#pipeline-summary-banner` if present.

Loaded ONLY on `/monitor` via `index.html`'s `{% block scripts %}`.

